  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 63. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 事例 — 実際にあった事柄の例。\n2. 人口 — ある地域に住んでいる人の数。\n3. 人材 — 力や技術などを生かして働く人。\n4. 人生 — 人が生きていく一生の歩み。\n5. 人体 — 人の体。\n6. 人名 — 人の名前。\n7. 人類 — 世界中の人間全体。\n8. 類推 — 似ていることを手掛かりに別のことを考えること。\n9. 累積 — 少しずつ重なって増えること。\n10. ルクス — 光が当たる面の明るさを表す単位。\n11. ルネサンス — ヨーロッパで古代の文化を見直して新しい文化が広がった動き。\n12. ルポルタージュ — 現地で調べた事実を伝える報告や文章。\n13. ルーフ — 屋根のこと。\n14. レイアウト — 文字や絵や物を見やすく配置すること。\n15. 零下 — 温度が零度より低いこと。\n16. 例外 — 普通の決まりに当てはまらないもの。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
